{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeCellular","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeCellular","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeTypeAPresentationEquiv"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.parabolicSym_mul_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.parabolicSym_mul_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L232-L237","doc":"The same on the right: `x · σ_i = q · x`. Identical content, since `1 · σ_i = σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_mul_parabolicSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_mul_parabolicSym","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L214-L230","doc":"**The defining eigenvector property**, left action: `σ_i · x = q · x`.\n\nThis is the quadratic relation rearranged — `σ_i + σ_i² = q σ_i + q` — and it is what\nmakes `x_λ` the right object to build the Murphy basis on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.parabolicSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.parabolicSym","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L209-L212","doc":"**The rank-one Murphy element** `x_{⟨s_i⟩} = 1 + σ_i`: the sum over the Young\nsubgroup generated by a single simple reflection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAIndexRep_ne_typeASignRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAIndexRep_ne_typeASignRep","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L159-L166","doc":"**The two extreme cell modules are distinct** as soon as there is a generator and\n`q ≠ −1`.\n\n`q = −1` is the first point where they collide, which is where semisimplicity of\n`H_n(q)` starts to fail — the reason the cellular machinery is needed at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeASignRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeASignRep","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L155-L157","doc":"The sign cell module: `σ_i ↦ −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAIndexRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.typeAIndexRep","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L151-L153","doc":"The index (trivial) cell module of the type-`A` Hecke algebra: `σ_i ↦ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.antiAut_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.antiAut_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L141-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.antiAut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.antiAut","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L90-L139","doc":"**The anti-automorphism fixing the generators**, as an algebra map into the opposite\nalgebra: Graham–Lehrer cellular axiom (C2) for the type-`A` Hecke algebra.\n\nThe three relation checks are the three rows of the table in the header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.T_quadratic_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.T_quadratic_swap","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L67-L84","doc":"The quadratic relation with the factors in the other order. Immediate from\n`T_quadratic` because `algebraMap` is central — and it is exactly the form the opposite\nalgebra asks for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.strandMatrix_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.strandMatrix_symm","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeCellular.lean#L55-L63","doc":"The type-`A` matrix is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0}]}